The base image carries every repo's toolchain. Resolve ALL dependencies during `docker build` (vendor / module cache / lockfile install): test runs may use `--no-network`, so nothing may be downloaded at run time.

`test_config.json` must be a JSON **list of suites**, one per repo/test kind, each with:

- `repo` — repo name from the table (test ids are namespaced `{repo}::{native id}` by the runner)
- `workdir` — directory the command runs in (e.g. `/workspace/<repo>`)
- `language`, `framework` — pick the matching parser (`pytest`, `go_test`, `cargo`, `jest`, ...)
- `run_cmd` (or `test_cmd`) — the test command; must write its report to `/output/{output_file}`
- `report_file` — optional output file name (`{state}` is substituted)
- `kind` — optional, `integration` for cross-repo/e2e suites

Do not merge repos into one tree and do not invent a combined `/testbed`.
